//! The pinned BSD system-call catalog, generated by `cargo xtask
//! darwin-catalogs` from xnu's `bsd/kern/syscalls.master`. Do not edit
//! by hand.
//!
//! Each row is the call's number, name, argument count (one 64-bit
//! register slot each under the arm64 LP64 ABI; `void` is zero) and
//! return-register munging, derived exactly as `makesyscalls.sh`
//! derives `sy_narg` and `sy_return_type`. Placeholder `enosys`/
//! `nosys` numbers are retained as reserved rows so the dispatcher
//! names them rather than treating them as absent.
